Cell["\<\
This notebooks demonstrates the algorithm implemented in deficiency.wl. The \
most important functions are:
* QuickDeficiencyIndices[poly_]: Returns the deficiency indices of poly_
* AdaptiveDeficiencyIndices[poly_]: The implementation of \
QuickDeficiencyIndices, displaying all the metadata and error codes
* DeficiencyPlot[poly_,z_,n_]: Returns the first n radia, ready to be plotted \
with list plot

We start by applying the algorithm on operators with known analytical \
results, then apply it onto operators from the literature, reproducing the \
table in the paper.
We proceed to sweep over parameters of an operator, reproducing the phase \
plot from the paper, and end with an exemplary plot of the radii.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016617330144377`*^9, 
  4.001662002851797*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a9a3b149-4391-4871-a48f-\
77b6e19a94a4"],

